  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-21T12:02:24.080Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, let me start by saying that yesterday my PC bluescreened while playing VRChat. It’s never bluescreened before. After the EAC update, it’s had memory errors only in VRChat. If I’m allowed to, I can link two pictures demonstrating what has happened (the BSOD and the game crash).\nThis is a huge issue. People said to me multiple times “oh, it’s your RAM!” but my PC has been incredibly stable otherwise in all scenarios. These memory errors only occur in VRChat, never in anything else, never outside of the game.\nEasy Anti-Cheat’s checks are pretty bad, and if it doesn’t like the environment you’re running the game in, boom- BSOD. \nCase example is one of my friend’s friends losing a homework assignment they were making because the anti cheat decided to crash their PC.\nRemember that Easy Anti-Cheat has full kernel level access, and can be programmed to to *wipe your drive and kill your hardware.*\nPlease don’t delete this post. It’s honest feedback, and a huge issue. If it’s fixed, I’ll happily play VRChat again. But for now, I am going to stay off the game as I would rather my PC not crash again. Maybe I’ll go on the Quest version for a bit. But seriously, this issue needs to be fixed.\n\nEdit: Removing the modules for competitive e-sport shooters should fix this issue entirely. Those modules are the root cause.",
